{"id": "EUVD-2026-55343", "enisaUuid": "ebe83334-25fc-391f-8008-a56144012387", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/i915/gt: Fix NULL deref on sched_engine alloc failure\n\nAvoid using intel_context_put() before intel_context_init() in\nexeclists_create_virtual() as the kref_put() inside would lead\nto NULL deref on the IOCTL path when sched_engine allocation fails.\n\nDiscovered using AI-assisted static analysis confirmed by\nIntel Product Security.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 4f2a12f2d50e9f48227656e4dcbd6423506be31d)", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:01:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:37", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bedeee4612afc15c53f8d3c6da05897506b4ca24", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7214db3e62fa9f0be7981cba9039bd835a79c070", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c174969f6af6c22fc9c51aefcdb7f9183c3a329a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/edd4804f07b8369ed472de19272974e2bf2a6271", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/82ec992c404c3dc774c5e9f3d4aa858e97187675"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4cj7-cqhw-3cg9", "CVE-2026-68242"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01a787b6-efd4-3862-8c4f-4f23aacb198d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3e28d37146db5dd49c469bc62a93ca791067d391 <bedeee4612afc15c53f8d3c6da05897506b4ca24"}, {"id": "327d5b0a-134d-3063-b806-2fbfd6d9a5b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "517b8d91-3562-37fd-bf9b-9937afd78c2b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "55186f96-38fc-3dfe-99e5-0189fbbf6971", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5ffe765d-f70d-3ca6-ab7f-6a2083e2b592", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "6566e30d-e387-34dc-9214-d4a940db9d51", "p